# Project Stack

Inventory MN is a Next.js App Router app. Prefer patterns that match these versions; do not introduce APIs from older major versions.

## Core

| Package                         | Version     | Role                                                  |
| ------------------------------- | ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| `next`                          | 16.2.9      | App Router, Server Components, Server Actions         |
| `react` / `react-dom`           | 19.2.4      | UI runtime                                            |
| `typescript`                    | ^5          | Strict typing (`strict: true`)                        |
| `eslint` / `eslint-config-next` | ^9 / 16.2.9 | Lint via `eslint` (not `next lint`)                   |
| `babel-plugin-react-compiler`   | 1.0.0       | Enabled via `reactCompiler: true` in `next.config.ts` |

**Next.js 16 / React 19 practices**

- Always `await` `cookies()`, `headers()`, `params`, and `searchParams` — sync access is removed.
- Prefer Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only for interactivity.
- Use Server Actions for mutations; keep secrets and JWT cookie work on the server.
- React Compiler is on: avoid adding `useMemo` / `useCallback` / `React.memo` unless profiling shows a real need.
- Turbopack is the default bundler; do not add Webpack-only config without cause.
- Require Node.js **20.9+**. Prefer `proxy.ts` over deprecated `middleware.ts` for network-edge logic.
- Caching is opt-in (`use cache` / Cache Components); do not assume fetch is cached by default.

## UI & styling

| Package                                | Version         | Role                                                         |
| -------------------------------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `tailwindcss` / `@tailwindcss/postcss` | ^4              | Utility CSS (PostCSS plugin only)                            |
| `tw-animate-css`                       | ^1.4.0          | Animations (replaces `tailwindcss-animate`)                  |
| `shadcn`                               | ^4.11.0         | CLI + CSS (`style: radix-nova`, RSC)                         |
| `radix-ui`                             | ^1.6.0          | Unified Radix primitives (`import { Slot } from "radix-ui"`) |
| `class-variance-authority`             | ^0.7.1          | Component variants                                           |
| `clsx` / `tailwind-merge`              | ^2.1.1 / ^3.6.0 | `cn()` helpers in `@/lib/utils`                              |
| `lucide-react`                         | ^1.21.0         | Icons (`iconLibrary: lucide`)                                |
| `next-themes`                          | ^0.4.6          | Theme switching                                              |
| `sonner`                               | ^2.0.7          | Toasts                                                       |

**UI practices**

- Configure Tailwind in CSS (`@import "tailwindcss"`, `@theme inline`, `@custom-variant dark`) — no `tailwind.config.js`.
- Keep design tokens in OKLCH CSS variables; extend via `@theme`, not a JS theme file.
- Add UI with the shadcn CLI into `@/components/ui`; compose with `cn()` and CVA.
- Import Radix from the `radix-ui` package (shadcn v4), not legacy `@radix-ui/react-*` packages.
- Use `toast` from `sonner` for user feedback after actions.

## Forms & validation

| Package               | Version | Role                      |
| --------------------- | ------- | ------------------------- |
| `zod`                 | ^4.4.3  | Schemas in `src/schemas/` |
| `react-hook-form`     | ^7.80.0 | Client forms              |
| `@hookform/resolvers` | ^5.4.0  | `zodResolver` bridge      |

**Form practices**

- Define schemas with Zod 4 APIs (`z.coerce`, `{ error: "..." }` message shape used in this repo).
- Prefer `import z from "zod"` to match existing schemas.
- Infer types with `z.infer` / `z.input`; wire forms with `Controller` + `zodResolver`.
- Validate again in Server Actions — never trust client-only checks.

## Domain utilities

| Package            | Version | Role                                         |
| ------------------ | ------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| `jsonwebtoken`     | ^9.0.3  | Decode JWT for cookie `maxAge` (server-only) |
| `@types/jsonwebtoken` | ^9.0.10 | Types                                     |
| `papaparse`        | ^5.5.4  | CSV import parsing                           |
| `@types/papaparse`  | ^5.5.2  | Types                                        |
| `jspdf`            | ^4.2.1  | Client-side PDF generation                   |
| `jspdf-autotable`  | ^5.0.8  | Tabular layouts for jsPDF                    |

**Utility practices**

- Keep JWT and cookie helpers in server modules (`"use server"` / server-only paths); set `httpOnly`, `sameSite: "strict"`, and `secure` in production.
- Parse CSV through shared helpers (e.g. `@/lib/parseCsvFile`); validate rows with Zod after parse.
- Export suggestion/inventory tables to PDF via `@/lib/exportSuggestInventoryPdf` (jsPDF + autoTable); keep PDF layout out of UI components.
- Do not add new heavy client libraries when Server Actions + existing utils suffice.

## Path aliases

Use `@/*` → `./src/*` (`@/components`, `@/lib`, `@/schemas`, `@/actions`, `@/services`).

## When adding dependencies

- Prefer packages already in this stack and matching major versions.
- After adding a library used in 3+ files, update this rule (see `self-improvement.mdc`).
